1.Develop visual assets for overseas markets （ North America, Southeast Asia), including digital campaigns, social media content, marketing materials, and in-store visuals;


2.Participate in campaign ideation and execution, ensuring strong and consistent brand visual identity;


3.Localize visual content based on cultural context across different regions to enhance engagement and effectiveness;


4.Collaborate closely with brand, marketing, PR, and local teams to support product launches, seasonal campaigns, and brand collaborations;


5.Establish and maintain overseas visual guidelines to ensure consistency across channels;


6.Stay updated on design trends and competitive landscape to continuously elevate brand aesthetics.


Qualifications：


1.Bachelor’s degree or above in Graphic Design, Visual Communication, Digital Media, or related fields;


2.Minimum 3 years of experience in visual design, with life-style brand-side experience preferred;


3.Strong sense of branding and aesthetics, with proven experience in end-to-end visual projects;


4.Proficient in design tools (e.g., Adobe Creative Suite); motion or video skills are a plus;


5.Strong cross-cultural awareness; overseas project experience is a plus;


6.Fluent in English (both written and spoken) as a working language;


7.Strong communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to work across time zones.

